---
import { RETENTION_DAYS } from "@trilleo/storage";
import InfoLayout from "../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../../lib/site";

const sections = [
  { slug: "ownership", text: "Who owns what" },
  { slug: "using", text: "Using the site’s content" },
  { slug: "report", text: "Reporting infringement" },
  { slug: "after", text: "What happens next" },
  { slug: "counter", text: "If your content was taken down" },
  { slug: "repeat", text: "Repeat infringement" },
  { slug: "trademarks", text: "Trademarks" },
] as const;
---

<InfoLayout path="/legal/copyright/" sections={sections} history>
  <h2 id="ownership">Who owns what</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The site’s writing, design, pictograms and games</strong>: ©
      Trilleo, unless a page says otherwise.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source code</strong>: open where its{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/Trilleo">GitHub repository</a> says so, under
      the licence stated there.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you post</strong> (comments, profiles, uploads, Minecraft
      creations): yours. The <a href="/legal/terms/#your-content">terms</a>{" "}
      describe the licence you give the site to show it; a creation’s own
      licence says what others may do with it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts and libraries</strong>: their authors’, used under their
      licences; see the <a href="/colophon/#credits">colophon</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="using">Using the site’s content</h2>
  <p>
    You’re welcome to quote posts, link to anything, and share screenshots, with
    a credit and a link back. Please ask before republishing whole posts or
    using the site’s images or pictograms elsewhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="report">Reporting infringement</h2>
  <p>
    If something on {SITE_NAME} uses your work without permission, tell me. The
    fastest way for a file is “Report this file” on its page, and for a
    Minecraft project “Report this project” (you’ll need to sign in). Otherwise,
    use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> (choose “Copyright or a
    takedown”) or email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Takedown`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>,
    with:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>your name and how to reach you;</li>
    <li>
      the work you own (or represent), and where the original can be seen;
    </li>
    <li>the address of each page or file on this site that infringes it;</li>
    <li>
      a statement that you believe in good faith the use isn’t allowed by you,
      your agent or the law, and that what you’ve written is accurate and you
      are the owner or allowed to act for them.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    This covers what notices need under China’s Regulations on the Protection of
    the Right to Network Dissemination of Information, and the US DMCA.
  </p>

  <h2 id="after">What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    A complete notice is usually acted on within a few days: the content is
    taken down (or access to it is disabled), and the person who posted it is
    told, with a copy of the notice minus your contact details if you ask. An
    incomplete or clearly mistaken notice gets a reply asking for more.
    Knowingly false notices can make you liable for the harm they cause.
  </p>

  <h2 id="counter">If your content was taken down</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe it was a mistake, or you have the right to use the work,
    appeal from <a href="/account/files/">your files</a>, or write to me with
    the address of the content, why you have the right to post it, and your
    contact details, which may be passed to the person who complained. If they
    don’t pursue it, the content can be restored. Taken-down files are kept for{" "}
    {RETENTION_DAYS.removed} days so that this is possible, then erased.
  </p>

  <h2 id="repeat">Repeat infringement</h2>
  <p>
    Each upload taken down for copyright normally counts as a strike, and
    accounts that keep infringing lose the ability to upload or are blocked, as
    the
    <a href="/legal/guidelines/#consequences">community guidelines</a> describe.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trademarks">Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Names and logos of other products mentioned on the site belong to their
    owners and are used only to refer to them. {SITE_NAME} is not an official
    Minecraft product, and is not approved by or associated with Mojang or
    Microsoft. GitHub is a trademark of GitHub, Inc.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
